      "observation": "The time derivative of the spatial integral equals the flux at the first endpoint minus the flux at the second endpoint."
    },
    {
      "location": "Raw PDF page 26; printed page 4, paragraph immediately following (1.10)",
      "anchor": "Each component of q measures the density of some conserved quantity",
      "observation": "The relation expresses componentwise conservation: the amount between the endpoints changes only through endpoint flux."
    },
    {
      "location": "Raw PDF page 26; printed page 4, first paragraph following (1.10)",
